  "notes": "Cause code is TBD/provisional per FORM-366 fields; narrative describes a blown fuse triggering an urgent failure alarm that was misinterpreted as a group demand indicator failure per TRM 8.1.3, leading to manual reactor trip breaker opening. Subsequent investigation confirmed the indicator was actually functional throughout. No backup systems modeled since all control rods fully inserted during the RPS actuation and no train of a safety system was rendered inoperable; AFW/Steam Dump removing decay heat is design-context, not a backup to the failed component. No previous similar events reported at SQN within three years, so no SIMILAR_TO/stub LER emitted."
